{"id":4682,"date":"2026-02-20T16:02:18","date_gmt":"2026-02-20T16:02:18","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/?p=4682"},"modified":"2026-03-30T15:27:22","modified_gmt":"2026-03-30T14:27:22","slug":"bristol-ccacs-south-west-hub-comes-of-age","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/bristol-ccacs-south-west-hub-comes-of-age\/","title":{"rendered":"Bristol: CCAC\u2019s South West hub comes of age"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-image stk-block-image stk-block stk-9a2b163\" data-block-id=\"9a2b163\"><style>.stk-9a2b163 {margin-bottom:14px !important;}<\/style><figure><span class=\"stk-img-wrapper stk-image--shape-stretch\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"stk-img wp-image-4740 lazyload\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Forest_Summer.png\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Forest_Summer.png 1920w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Forest_Summer-300x169.png 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Forest_Summer-1024x576.png 1024w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Forest_Summer-768x432.png 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Forest_Summer-1536x864.png 1536w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Forest_Summer-356x200.png 356w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Forest_Summer-200x113.png 200w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 1920px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 1920\/1080;\" \/><\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-text stk-block-text stk-block stk-49a5808\" data-block-id=\"49a5808\"><style>.stk-49a5808 {margin-bottom:0px !important;}.stk-49a5808 .stk-block-text__text{font-size:12px !important;}@media screen and (max-width: 1023px){.stk-49a5808 .stk-block-text__text{font-size:12px !important;}}@media screen and (max-width: 767px){.stk-49a5808 .stk-block-text__text{font-size:10px !important;}}<\/style><p class=\"stk-block-text__text\"><em>Rendering: Sylva Studio<\/em><\/p><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><br>The\u00a0South West\u00a0hub\u00a0was set up in 2023 with a single collaboration between Bristol&#8217;s Ashton Gate Primary School\u00a0and\u00a0designers Finbar Charleson and Jack Cardno (Sylva Studio). Three further successful co-designs followed, one as far afield as Mevagissey in Cornwall. We are now planning a further sixteen across the region. As the vanguard\u00a0of CCAC\u2019s expansion,\u00a0the South West hub will stand as the blueprint for other nascent hubs.\u00a0<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Manchester for\u00a0the North West and Derby for the East Midlands\u00a0are following closely behind. London and the South East, our starting point, remains the most advanced.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">To widen our reach and deepen our impact, regional hubs prioritise local identity and expertise. Each develops a distinctive presence, leveraging&nbsp;regional networks and local knowledge&nbsp;and&nbsp;address the specific&nbsp;extreme&nbsp;climate&nbsp;risks&nbsp;local to their communities.&nbsp;We partner with&nbsp;both&nbsp;established design practices,&nbsp;who contribute their time&nbsp;<em>pro bono,<\/em>&nbsp;and sponsored&nbsp;emerging talent&nbsp;secured through&nbsp;the CCAC Young Designer\u2019s Award.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/MG_0240-2-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-4745 lazyload\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/MG_0240-2-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/MG_0240-2-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/MG_0240-2-768x512.jpg 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/MG_0240-2-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/MG_0240-2-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/MG_0240-2-188x125.jpg 188w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 1024px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 1024\/683;\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Aurelie Fontan conducting a screen-printing workshop with Year-5 Gorran Primary School pupils<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">The next stage of the South West initiative is underway at Headley Park Primary School. We are incredibly pleased to welcome Arup and Stride Treglown for an inspiring community regeneration collaboration set in future extreme conditions located on land lying between the school and the surrounding community. The co-design allows pupils to work alongside industry experts to gain climate and design learning, and to reimagine a familiar setting in unpredictable times.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Leading this regional expansion is our Development Manager, Pieta&nbsp;Karoniemi. Based in Bristol, Pieta is building a robust network of local schools, designers, and other community stakeholders.&nbsp;She says, \u201c<em>We need to&nbsp;give&nbsp;primary school children a positive understanding&nbsp;of their uncertain future. Achieving this through the lens of creative design feels hopeful and inspiring.\u201d&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/em>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Get Involved:<\/strong>&nbsp;Do you know a school or a designer in the South West who might like to&nbsp;participate? Please&nbsp;contact&nbsp;Pieta at <a href=\"mailto:pieta@cc-ac.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><strong>pieta@cc-ac.org<\/strong><\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>CCAC\u2019s South West hub expands with a new Arup and Stride Treglown partnership at Headley Park Primary, setting the blue print for regional climate co-design hubs.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":10,"featured_media":4740,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[12],"tags":[5,19,27,6,38,39,37],"class_list":["post-4682","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-ccac-news","tag-climate","tag-co-design","tag-designer","tag-education","tag-hub","tag-region","tag-southwest"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.5 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/product\/yoast-seo-wordpress\/ -->\n<title>Bristol: CCAC\u2019s South West hub comes of age - Climate Change All Change<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"CCAC\u2019s Southwest hub expands with a new Arup and Stride Treglown partnership at Headley Park Primary, setting the blueprint for regional climate co-design hubs.\" \/>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/bristol-ccacs-south-west-hub-comes-of-age\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_GB\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Bristol: CCAC\u2019s South West hub comes of age - Climate Change All Change\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"CCAC\u2019s Southwest hub expands with a new Arup and Stride Treglown partnership at Headley Park Primary, sett